# Shared by `make format`, `make format-check` and the CI format job, so all three
# agree. Without the excludes, SwiftFormat descends into whatever Xcode generated or
# checked out under a derived data directory and reformats third-party sources, so the
# globs cover the generated paths themselves rather than relying on the directory name.

--swiftversion 6.0.3

--exclude **/DerivedData*/**,**/.build/**,Sparkle/**,**/Build/Intermediates.noindex/**,**/DerivedSources/**,**/SourcePackages/**
